counteract:
And then I go the furthest off
To counteract a knock;
Then draw my little letter forth

country:
Explored the trains, enquired among the ships,
And felt the country through from end to end;
No Marian!—Though I hinted what I knew,—

cough:
Ez if de day was made fu' sleep;
Hit's funny when you got a cough
Somehow yo' voice seems too fu' off--

coupling:
No lily-muffled hum of a summer-bee,
But finds some coupling with the spinning stars;
No pebble at your foot, but proves a sphere;

cousins:
And fain would know the end of everything,
Of cousins, therefore, with the rest. For me,
Aurora, I’ve my work; you know my work;

courteously:
Of the dead singer of Senlac, and his smile.
Shyly and courteously he smiled and spoke;
"I've been in the laurel since the winter broke;

coursed:
Curbed his amber-bitted steed,
Coursed amain to hear;
All his princes in his train,

cou't:
I t'ink of huh at mornin' an' I dream of huh at night;
But how's I gwine to cou't huh w'en I do' know how to write?
Oh, my; oh, my.

cou'tin:
Hangin' 'roun' my Mary;
Cou'tin' boun' to prospah
W'en hit's wa'm in Febawary.

coursers:
Beyond the flood in sacred annals told,
And the great sage, + whom fiery coursers drew
To heav'n's bright portals from Elisha's view;

courser's:
While in his breast he feels the shaft of death;
He drops the bridle on his courser's mane,
Before his eyes in shadows swims the plain,

courtesy's:
He half turned away, then he quite turned back:
For courtesy's sake he could not lack
To redeem his own royal pledge;

counterpoint:
We beat the phorminx till we hurt our thumbs,
As if still ignorant of counterpoint;
We call the Muse.... ‘O Muse, benignant Muse!’—

counterfeiting:
Against the heels of what the master said;
And counterfeiting epics, shrill with trumps
A babe might blow between two straining cheeks
